        "content": "<p>The PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43912\">#43912</a> ensures that <code>public import Mathlib</code> does not have the effect of exposing Lean internals to our downstream users: i.e. if they want to do metaprogramming, they need to either be using <code>meta def</code>, or to explicitly do a <code>public import Lean.XYZ</code>.</p>\n<p>The goal is not to force users who want to <code>import Mathlib</code> to have Lean internals in their public scope.</p>\n<p>(This then gives downstream libraries the possibility of relying on this invariant, if they want to audit or restrict the use of metaprogramming.)</p>\n<p>This PR makes many small adjustments to Mathlib imports , essentially all of the form <code>public import X ~~&gt; public meta import X</code>. But the key step is adding a test file with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Invalid definition `foo`, may not access declaration `Lean.Expr.bvar` imported as `meta`; consider adding `import Lean.Expr`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- The same API remains usable inside a `meta def`:</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elaboratedExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and a second test file showing that if the user adds the relevant <code>public import Lean.XYZ</code> then things work as expected:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 628584692,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1790925741
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that after this is merged the following (at least) PR will acquire merge conflicts, and other metaprogramming related PRs may need to be aware of this new invariant.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44390\">#44390</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44383\">#44383</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44373\">#44373</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44367\">#44367</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44344\">#44344</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44343\">#44343</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44342\">#44342</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44332\">#44332</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44323\">#44323</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44135\">#44135</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43802\">#43802</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43692\">#43692</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43438\">#43438</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42572\">#42572</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42563\">#42563</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42536\">#42536</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42519\">#42519</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42452\">#42452</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41245\">#41245</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40852\">#40852</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40114\">#40114</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39207\">#39207</a></p>",
